DONE: reading is robust.
  - PIO flux_reader measures full period (pulse + gap)
  - CRC-16/CCITT on ID and data fields
  - Static PLL with half-cell tracking
  - 500ms read timeout, single external retry
  - Core 0: USB MSC + CDC debug + LED (RGB)
  - Core 1: pure floppy I/O, no peripherals
  - Step 3ms/3ms, settling 8ms, motor spin-up 500ms
  - DIP switch mode flags (debug/write/greasweasel)
  - WP pin + DIP switch write-protect layering
  - Composite USB device (MSC + CDC ACM)
  - DEBUG.md reference for serial output

DONE: write corruption fixes (4 bugs)
  1. emit_byte_a1() bit4: clock present [1,0] -> should be absent [0,0]
  2. PIO out_shift direction: shift_right=true output LSB-first but
     encoder packs MSB-first, reversing every 32-bit word.
  3. Second CRC byte prev chaining: used (crc>>7)&1 instead of (crc>>8)&1
  4. PIO clock divider: clkdiv=10 gave 1us half-cells, but decoder
     PLL=200 targets 2us. Changed to clkdiv=20.

DONE: GreaseWeasel raw flux mode (DIP bit 2)
  - Full GW protocol via CDC ACM: 22 commands implemented
  - Flux read (CMD_READ_FLUX): index-synced + ticks_limit + RPM modes
  - Revs-based capture with 160KB RAM buffer, greasepack encoding
  - Hardware GPIO IRQ-based index pulse detection
  - IRQ-based index detection restored in revs-based capture (was polling)
  - Pin-level noise filter on index accept (gpio_get==0 check)
  - gw read: working on all tracks, sectors decoding confirmed
  - RPM mode: correct on all disks (synthetic flux from index pulse timing,
    avoids RDATA-to-INDEX crosstalk by not using real PIO flux data)
  - gw seek / gw info: functional
  - SET_PARAMS / GET_PARAMS: 8x uint16 delay parameters implemented
  - GET_INDEX_TIMES: proper implementation
  - ERASE_FLUX: write-protect check + configurable motor delay
  - FluxEngine: reads and decodes sectors
  - USB descriptors: VID 0x1209 PID 0x4d69, "gw-compat" product string
  - Serial number from RP2040 unique board ID
  - 10s motor auto-off watchdog
  - CDC TX buffer increased to 512 bytes

DONE: CMD_WRITE_FLUX protocol fixes (2024-06)
  - greaseunpack 2-byte decoding formula corrected (was base-250, now
    proper base-255: (data-250)*255+(data2-1)+250)
  - gw_init_writer: only disables SM if currently claimed
  - TX FIFO pre-load: single short pulse (~4.7us) instead of 4x1.3ms
  - dv minimum clamp: dv<2 -> dv=2 (prevents PIO jmp x-- infinite loop)
  - WDATA restored to HIGH after write (was left LOW by stalled PIO)
  - gw_writer SM fully released (unclaimed + program removed) after write
  - Write-to-read recovery delay: 200ms sleep after WGATE drop
  - Read capture loops: added 5s deadline timeouts (prevents lockups)
  - Revs-based capture: restored hardware IRQ index detection (was polling)
  - Revs-based capture: added gpio_get(PIN_INDEX)==0 noise filter to
    prevent RDATA crosstalk glitches from being accepted as index pulses

FIXED (2024-06-22): immediate read-after-write verify failure
  - Root cause: `cc` (capture index) was `uint16_t`, silently wrapping at
    65535. The buffer-limit check `cc < GW_FLUX_CAP_WORDS (80000)` was
    always true because cc wrapped before reaching 80000. The buffer
    endlessly self-overwrote, and only the last ~65536 entries (~89ms)
    were sent to the host.
  - Fix: changed `cc` from `uint16_t` to `uint32_t` in all three capture
    paths (ticks-limit, revs-based, RPM-mode).
  - Buffer increased: 80000 → 105000 entries (210KB) provides ~210ms
    at typical 2us pulse density, covering a full revolution with margin.
  - Cleanup: removed experimental code. Post-write sleep set to 20ms.

DONE: MSC cross-core robustness
  - shared_sector_buffer now volatile (prevents compiler reordering
    across __dmb() barriers)
  - force_recalibrate flag replaces direct cross-core write to current_track
  - Removed dead shared variables (shared_fmt_rd_ok, gw_busy, etc.)
  - ID CRC validation added for write_physical_sector sector header match
  - Pre-write / post-write delays use configurable values
  - GAP4b fill added to format_track_encode, bp_flush zero-fill fix
  - MSC read robustness: sync-loss hysteresis (4 consecutive bad pulses),
    1000ms timeout, jiggle retry (step away+back on second failure)
  - Sector cache: single-sector read cache for FAT/directory re-reads
  - set_density(true) on motor start for HD density

DONE: GW RPM mode restored for rotational period measurement
  - time_us_32() polling gives deterministic RPM (no PIO FIFO latency)
  - Multi-rev data reads still use real PIO + hardware IRQ index detection

FIXED (2026-10-04): MSC sector write path (hardware validation pending)
  - Equal 20-cycle PIO branches: pulse bits no longer fall through into the
    no-pulse delay. 1 us half-cells at 20 MHz; LOW pulses are 200 ns.
  - MSB-first packing and left-shifting PIO agree for sector and format data.
  - A1 missing-clock mark is 0x4489 (missing clock at data bit 2).
  - DMA feeds a finite stream; PIO IRQ, not FIFO empty, confirms completion.
  - CRC-valid ID lookup, standard GAP2 alignment and per-sector readback.
  - FORMAT uses index period, correct gaps/IAM, a guard and verification.
  - Failed/timed-out requests keep buffer ownership until core 1 finishes.
  - Native encoding/decoding, writer failure and assembled PIO timing tests.

FIXED (2026-10-04): sustained MSC transfer hangs (hardware validation pending)
  - Debug CDC writes no longer spin on a full TX FIFO inside USB callbacks.
  - MSC callbacks yield while core 1 is busy; USB can service CDC and resets.
  - A fixed sector buffer is retained through retries, timeouts and resets.
  - Allocate the 210 KB flux buffer only in GreaseWeasel mode and allocate
    the format track stream only while formatting; static BSS is 10,508 bytes.
  - Host regression keeps CDC full through 150 KiB + 1 MiB read/write transfers.

CHANGED (2026-10-04): follow-up for repeatable LBA 81/82 stalls
  - Bound each USB task run to 16 queue receives so self-queued MSC retries
    cannot starve application polling. Preserve Pico queue/lock primitives.
  - Route GW USB service loops through the same bounded entry point.
  - Floppy worker delays use direct timer waits rather than core 0 alarms.
  - Debug banner identifies msc-progress-v3; pending I/O logs its stage once
    per second, and WRITE verified identifies successful worker completion.
  - Host tests cover 1,000 continuously busy USB task runs and stage reports.
  - The exact hardware freeze remains unconfirmed; retest and capture logs.

DROPPED (was uint16_t cc bug, not hardware):
  - Index RPM detection via real PIO flux data showing ~2500 RPM.
    The cc overflow corrupted index positions and flux data.
    Fixed by the uint16_t → uint32_t cc change.

